kernelbase: implement FlsGetValue2, the newer FLS lookup UCRT/VCRuntime
probe for and call unconditionally when found.

Missing on upstream Wine (11.0 and later) and on CrossOver's own build too
(checked directly) — a real Wine gap. Newer UCRT/VCRuntime builds (e.g.
Unity games, see frankea/Whisky#258) call FlsGetValue2() from a hot path
expecting the calling thread's last-error code left untouched, unlike
FlsGetValue(), and crash when it is missing.

Same shape as FlsGetValue(), routing straight to RtlFlsGetValue() (which
never touches last-error) instead of through set_ntstatus() (which does).

--- a/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c	2026-09-27 23:20:07
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c	2026-09-27 23:20:07
@@ -1308,6 +1308,24 @@
 
     if (!set_ntstatus( RtlFlsGetValue( index, &data ))) return NULL;
     SetLastError( ERROR_SUCCESS );
+    return data;
+}
+
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           FlsGetValue2   (kernelbase.@)
+ *
+ * Newer Windows-internal variant of FlsGetValue(), missing from Wine (and
+ * from real Windows on older builds too): newer UCRT/VCRuntime builds probe
+ * for it via GetProcAddress and call it from a hot path that must not
+ * disturb the calling thread's last-error code, unlike FlsGetValue(), and
+ * crash when it is missing (e.g. Unity games).
+ */
+PVOID WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH FlsGetValue2( DWORD index )
+{
+    void *data;
+
+    if (!NT_SUCCESS( RtlFlsGetValue( index, &data ))) return NULL;
     return data;
 }
 
